    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"02. Gauss–Seidel: a sequential in-place sweep\"\ndescription: \"Each update reads values updated a moment earlier in the same sweep. Natural as a loop, awkward as an array program.\"\njupyter: python3\n---\n\n\n\n## The problem\n\nSolve $-\\Delta u = \\theta$ on the unit square ($n \\times n$ interior points, $u = 0$ on the\nboundary) with $K$ Gauss–Seidel sweeps from $u = 0$, and differentiate\n$$\\mathcal{L}(\\theta) = \\lVert u_K(\\theta) - u_{\\text{obs}} \\rVert^2$$\nwith respect to the source $\\theta$. Each update is\n$$u_{ij} \\leftarrow \\tfrac14\\left(h^2\\theta_{ij} + u_{i-1,j} + u_{i+1,j} + u_{i,j-1} + u_{i,j+1}\\right),$$\n**in place**: $u_{i-1,j}$ and $u_{i,j-1}$ are values already updated earlier in the\nsame sweep. That is what makes Gauss–Seidel converge about twice as fast as Jacobi,\nand it is what makes it a sequential loop.\n\nThe same pattern appears in SOR, incomplete factorisations, the Thomas algorithm,\nupwind sweeps and line relaxation.\n\nTwo variants:\n\n- **Lexicographic**, the textbook sweep: a triple loop.\n- **Red-black**, which colours the grid like a chessboard so that each colour can be\n  updated in parallel. It is a *different iteration*, with a different result, and it is\n  the formulation a GPU or JAX user writes. Gradients are compared within each variant.\n\n## Code\n\n::: {.panel-tabset group=\"impl\"}\n## Enzyme.jl\nLexicographic, CPU:\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#loss-lex echo=true >}}\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#grad-lex echo=true >}}\n\nRed-black, KernelAbstractions (CPU and GPU):\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#loss-rb echo=true >}}\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#grad-rb echo=true >}}\n\n## JAX\nLexicographic:\n{{< embed jax.qmd#loss-lex echo=true >}}\n{{< embed jax.qmd#grad-lex echo=true >}}\n\nRed-black:\n{{< embed jax.qmd#loss-rb echo=true >}}\n{{< embed jax.qmd#grad-rb echo=true >}}\n\n## Reactant.jl\nLexicographic:\n{{< embed reactant.qmd#loss-lex echo=true >}}\n\nRed-black:\n{{< embed reactant.qmd#loss-rb echo=true >}}\n{{< embed reactant.qmd#grad echo=true >}}\n:::\n\n## Same gradient\n\n$n = 32$, $K = 20$, Float64. Each gradient is also checked against finite differences.\n\n::: {#ad3ccfd6 .cell execution_count=2}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n</style>\n<table id=\"T_016a5\">\n  <caption>lexicographic</caption>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th id=\"T_016a5_level0_col0\" class=\"col_heading level0 col0\" >implementation</th>\n      <th id=\"T_016a5_level0_col1\" class=\"col_heading level0 col1\" >‖g‖₂</th>\n      <th id=\"T_016a5_level0_col2\" class=\"col_heading level0 col2\" >max rel. diff vs enzyme-lex</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row0_col0\" class=\"data row0 col0\" >enzyme-lex</td>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row0_col1\" class=\"data row0 col1\" >6.409859e-04</td>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row0_col2\" class=\"data row0 col2\" >0.0e+00</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row1_col0\" class=\"data row1 col0\" >reactant-lex</td>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row1_col1\" class=\"data row1 col1\" >6.409859e-04</td>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row1_col2\" class=\"data row1 col2\" >4.3e-16</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row2_col0\" class=\"data row2 col0\" >jax-lex</td>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row2_col1\" class=\"data row2 col1\" >6.409859e-04</td>\n      <td id=\"T_016a5_row2_col2\" class=\"data row2 col2\" >2.1e-16</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n</style>\n<table id=\"T_656dc\">\n  <caption>red-black</caption>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th id=\"T_656dc_level0_col0\" class=\"col_heading level0 col0\" >implementation</th>\n      <th id=\"T_656dc_level0_col1\" class=\"col_heading level0 col1\" >‖g‖₂</th>\n      <th id=\"T_656dc_level0_col2\" class=\"col_heading level0 col2\" >max rel. diff vs enzyme-rb</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row0_col0\" class=\"data row0 col0\" >enzyme-rb</td>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row0_col1\" class=\"data row0 col1\" >6.366981e-04</td>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row0_col2\" class=\"data row0 col2\" >0.0e+00</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row1_col0\" class=\"data row1 col0\" >reactant-rb</td>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row1_col1\" class=\"data row1 col1\" >6.366981e-04</td>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row1_col2\" class=\"data row1 col2\" >5.4e-16</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row2_col0\" class=\"data row2 col0\" >jax-rb</td>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row2_col1\" class=\"data row2 col1\" >6.366981e-04</td>\n      <td id=\"T_656dc_row2_col2\" class=\"data row2 col2\" >4.3e-16</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Timings\n\n$K = 100$ sweeps, Float64, median of 3–10 runs after warm-up. A sweep stops once a\nsingle gradient takes more than 5 s.\n\n::: {#f2212226 .cell execution_count=3}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\">                        <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"a13b54ba-49b1-4b71-bd0f-4119c9870534\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"a13b54ba-49b1-4b71-bd0f-4119c9870534\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"a13b54ba-49b1-4b71-bd0f-4119c9870534\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"implementation=enzyme \\u002f lexicographic (cpu)\\u003cbr\\u003egrid points n²=%{x}\\u003cbr\\u003egradient time [s]=%{y}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"legendgroup\":\"enzyme \\u002f